at a positive angle is measured counter-clockwise.\n\nTherefore, the correct diagram is as follows:\n\n![](images/72/72030fb9fe1e92b8be67d4a4cf2c899c83ba1242892231f18925c2354a143bdc.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527203 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50de296d-56a1-5166-aa7d-42de027a33bc" :knowledge-point/title "Using Trigonometry to Find an Angle in the Coordinate Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1dc087e2-0dbe-5157-ba6b-1c3b2fefb15b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526564} {:answer/id #uuid "71ff9bb7-a425-576c-95a3-1135fc029967" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{35}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526724} {:answer/id #uuid "daa05632-592e-54c0-bc54-0039b3767877" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{60}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526926} {:answer/id #uuid "e1a66eda-15a4-5835-97f8-9fb6a90c3584" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526944} {:answer/id #uuid "f3668ebd-cf52-5aea-abde-8afb6d8922f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{40}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526986}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1a66eda-15a4-5835-97f8-9fb6a90c3584" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526944} :answer-field/id #uuid "5397a46c-0c2d-53f8-ab44-aceeab82183b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527053}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ba6955a5-f1b2-5bb6-bbb0-ee805b7e5b79" :question/math-academy-id "q-123640" :question/problem "![](images/ca/caacb6ef264b8f7862a893b4127704e46e66d33a212b53017e8bde4e32fa3004.png)\n\nGiven that the point $A$ has coordinates $(\\sqrt{6},\\sqrt{2}),$ calculate the angle $\\theta .$" :question/worked-solution "We can form a triangle by creating a vertical line from $A$ to the $x$-axis.\n\n![](images/43/432dbcd0967ba40a5f477d30c8e9b0985c8151fb2f13e54ad346cff4ac20c1c5.png)\n\nUsing the tangent ratio, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the inverse tangent, we get\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})={30}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527215 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50de296d-56a1-5166-aa7d-42de027a33bc" :knowledge-point/title "Using Trigonometry to Find an Angle in the Coordinate Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27b2a7ea-ce2a-5a6a-92f8-768240562e5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526588} {:answer/id #uuid "34f6f6a5-375f-5a26-9bce-bdeb0161b913" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526604} {:answer/id #uuid "81bc51d2-b781-5ce6-bee1-3aca60f8e68f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526764} {:answer/id #uuid "bc4dd9aa-13a0-5eca-a4d7-fa0619b54902" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526864} {:answer/id #uuid "c32cb09d-14d8-594b-92c6-be98876a3257" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526874}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34f6f6a5-375f-5a26-9bce-bdeb0161b913" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526604} :answer-field/id #uuid "952ffaa2-6445-557f-8ebf-48e76ada3f05" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527076}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d86e19a0-8ae0-5dcf-aad3-3a9ae2b60335" :question/math-academy-id "q-123891" :question/problem "![](images/08/08ee9a92a96f2ab0e4644dc02dfd4be605e72e9b778f54bf60d8e4014d58a7bd.png)\n\nGiven that the point $A$ has coordinates $(-3\\sqrt{3},9)$, calculate the angle $\\theta .$" :question/worked-solution "We can form a triangle by creating a vertical line from $A$ to the $x$-axis. Let us call ${\\theta }^{′}$ the acute angle that is supplementary to $\\theta .$\n\n![](images/e0/e0643cdb2d864b3af6466e24ab815dc8085e811dfdb86cdce253981a521faf82.png)\n\nUsing the tangent ratio, we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡{\\theta }^{′}=\\frac{9}{3\\sqrt{3}}=\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3}}=\\sqrt{3}.\n$$\n\nFinally, using the inverse tangent, we get\n\n$$\n{\\theta }^{′}=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\sqrt{3}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\theta +{\\theta }^{′}=\\pi ,$ then $\\theta =\\pi -{\\theta }^{′}=\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3}=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120317 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50de296d-56a1-5166-aa7d-42de027a33bc" :knowledge-point/title "Using Trigonometry to Find an Angle in the Coordinate Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e2ac522-64d7-594c-a927-f8e2ee384d62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{62}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526532} {:answer/id #uuid "16520806-5ceb-5aeb-953d-8cbc11369ac2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{50}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526548} {:answer/id #uuid "829ddc9b-e6e9-52d8-b401-9537caed6cdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{60}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526765} {:answer/id #uuid "d01e780e-2766-5f8c-8877-8808a159b6e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{55}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526903} {:answer/id #uuid "dc56464e-9f0f-5fa7-bbbe-4b15d3b4618a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{65}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526930}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "829ddc9b-e6e9-52d8-b401-9537caed6cdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{60}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526765} :answer-field/id #uuid "116b0a49-5e8a-5bd3-8573-7f0ffe6f1626" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118041}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6b5c3cfe-f2c4-5a54-b666-7bc318db7b5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-34270" :question/problem "![](images/fb/fb2876d08dc2aa17b42d137b6d1a486447995e7d52edd37846e9c040265dc1bc.png)\n\nGiven that the point $A$ has coordinates $(1,\\sqrt{3}),$ calculate the angle $\\theta .$" :question/worked-solution "We can form a triangle by creating a vertical line from $A$ to the $x$-axis.\n\n![](images/d4/d4aa760fae46877c78d0bb2b87b7b047832a2600258401af1d021f693bb788b3.png)\n\nUsing the tangent ratio, we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{1}=\\sqrt{3}.\n$$\n\nUsing the inverse tangent, we get\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\sqrt{3}={60}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [