rac{5}{4},-\\frac{5}{4}),$ calculate the angle $\\theta .$" :question/worked-solution "We can form a triangle by creating a vertical line from $A$ to the $x$-axis. Let us call ${\\theta }^{′}$ the acute angle that is formed with the $x$-axis such that ${\\theta }^{′}+{180}^{∘}=\\theta $\n\n![](images/e3/e3abf66be20a5ab3ed5d0b8812b127d6336cb88f8369937d415c8918d020e45e.png)\n\nUsing the tangent ratio, we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡{\\theta }^{′}=\\frac{(\\frac{5}{4})}{(\\frac{5}{4})}=1.\n$$\n\nFinally, using the inverse tangent, we get\n\n$$\n{\\theta }^{′}=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡1={45}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nFinally, using $\\theta ={\\theta }^{′}+{180}^{∘},$ we get $\\theta ={45}^{∘}+{180}^{∘}={225}^{∘}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120337 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119754 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "04ac62a3-1302-5011-937b-9fb20cb7fe95" :knowledge-point/title "Representing Angles in the Coordinate Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8155491c-18c2-5103-adc2-de10a40a126b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/21/219e92b0fa9b90a47d050c0be6541b0648a2106ec66ac39f91e391b2d58956da.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118152} {:answer/id #uuid "badb1f9f-3482-514a-9203-664992158758" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b6/b61cb7cf870ffaba816badaabadae1de14001b584f4994d79ed74c114413485d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118153} {:answer/id #uuid "ce6fd9ed-5a54-5841-a2c9-c8a754e65254" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d4/d42d091f0c2b81b5a07bf3f13494cd6ce11b05c07838c7b10cddd1f697d95bec.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118154} {:answer/id #uuid "fcfb466c-03f6-52f8-9ccd-b59dd1f75d5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/53/53bdd11d4204beb60f0b705693ed4d0d75f6a3e26bc3a593b0147852be4baa97.png" :db/i